## 8. Behavior
### 8.1 Search criteria
- THE SYSTEM SHALL render the Search Criteria panel with fields Configuration ID, Configuration Name, Owner Name, Owner Module, and Protocol. [asset:sections/02-pagebody.png, kit:k1, kit:k2, kit:k3]
- WHEN the user clicks Search (`nextButton`) THE SYSTEM SHALL show the Search Results panel (`h2`) and apply filters to `#FileTransferSearchGrid` using the current criteria values. [ctl:nextButton, kit:k4, js:Scripts/FileTransfer/hp.ua3.FileTransfer.searchSourceLocations__884a35a7.js#performFileTransferSearch]
- WHEN the user clicks Create New (`FileTransferGridAddButton`) THE SYSTEM SHALL open modal overlay `FileTransferConfigurationEditPopup`. [ctl:FileTransferGridAddButton, kit:d1, js:Scripts/FileTransfer/hp.ua3.FileTransfer.searchSourceLocations__884a35a7.js#(FileTransferGridAddButton).click]
- WHEN the user clicks Reset (`resetButton`) THE SYSTEM SHALL reset the form, clear the results grid data, and hide the Search Results panel. [ctl:resetButton, js:Scripts/FileTransfer/hp.ua3.FileTransfer.searchSourceLocations__884a35a7.js#resetSearchFileTransfer]
- WHEN the user clicks Cancel (`cancelButton`) THE SYSTEM SHALL leave this screen. [ctl:cancelButton, UNKNOWN: destination and whether it prompts]

### 8.2 Search results
- WHILE `resultsVisible` is false THE SYSTEM SHALL keep `#searchFileTransferConfigResultsPanel` hidden (`display:none`). [asset:snapshot/rendered.html]
- WHEN results are shown THE SYSTEM SHALL display grid columns: Configuration ID, Configuration Name, Protocol, Address, Mask, Owner Name, Owner Module, Status, Fts Source Location Id (hidden by default). [kit:k4, asset:snapshot/rendered.html]
- WHEN the user toggles ?Show Inactives? (`FileTransferShowInactiveCheckBox`) THE SYSTEM SHALL clear general messages and re-apply filters to `#FileTransferSearchGrid`. [ctl:FileTransferShowInactiveCheckBox, js:Scripts/FileTransfer/hp.ua3.FileTransfer.searchSourceLocations__884a35a7.js#applyFileTransferFilter]
- WHEN the user single-clicks a results row THE SYSTEM SHALL select the row and set `ftsSourceLocationId` from the row?s `FtsSourceLocationId`. [kit:k4, js:Scripts/FileTransfer/hp.ua3.FileTransfer.searchSourceLocations__884a35a7.js#fileTransferGridOnRowSelected]
- WHEN the user double-clicks a results row THE SYSTEM SHALL open modal overlay `FileTransferConfigurationViewOverlay` (dialog `d2`). [kit:k4, kit:d2, js:Scripts/FileTransfer/hp.ua3.FileTransfer.searchSourceLocations__884a35a7.js#onDisplayFileTransferView]

### 8.3 Dialogs
- WHEN dialog `d1` is open THE SYSTEM SHALL show required-field indicators (magenta `*`) for required fields. [kit:d1, asset:kit/states/dialog-d1.png]
- WHEN dialog `d2` is open THE SYSTEM SHALL present fields as read-only and disable checkboxes (where `disabled=true`). [kit:d2, asset:kit/states/dialog-d2.png]
- THE SYSTEM SHALL render the Destination grid in `d1` with columns: Destination Address, Destination Protocol, Contact Name, Status, Active, Contact Phone, Contact Email, Overwrite At Destination, Compress At Destination, Destination Is Archive, Rename At Destination, Rename Pattern, Server, Destination Id, Destination Line Number, Is Added Updated, FTE Metadata, FTE Module Contract, Destination Type. [kit:k12, kit:d1]
- THE SYSTEM SHALL render the Destination grid in `d2` with columns: Destination Address, Destination Protocol, Contact Name, Status (with `Active` hidden). [kit:k39, kit:d2]

